## Observed proof

- apps/linux: `fmt --check`, `clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`,
  `build --locked`, `check --locked`, `test --locked` all exit 0; 58 tests pass.
- the handshake-advertised limits are logged by the data plane:
  `max_concurrent_streams=8 credit_window_bytes=262144`.
- `session.create` → `block.attach` (WRITER, `takeover: false`) on the data plane:
  stream_id 1; the deterministic command and initial `stty size` are observed.
- `terminal.resize` (cols=120 rows=40, pane pixels 1200x800) accepted by the
  server: `TerminalResizeAccepted = stream_id=1 cols=120 rows=40`; the child's
  own `stty size` then reports `40 120`.
- two concurrent streams on one data-plane connection (stream_id 1 and 2); the
  second stream's burst of 400384 bytes (larger than the 256 KiB per-stream
  credit window) is delivered in 104 frames at 9.4 MB/s and the connection
  survives; `RELAYABLE-PROBE-ALIVE` on the first stream proves it is still usable
  afterwards.
- `PROBE_EXIT=0`.
